From 0832113f971a76ae4342fa3f74300b391acdf750 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lakr233 <git@qaq.wiki>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 10:15:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 66/68] vgpu: support XR10 and two-plane alpha on IOSurface
 mappings

Two-plane RGB10A8_2p_XR10 (0x226/0x227) IOSurfaces store extended-range
10-bit RGB in Plane 0 and 8-bit alpha in Plane 1. Previously, IOSurface
render writeback narrowed XR10 targets through BGRA8 and wrote Plane 0
only, leaving Plane 1 alpha zeroed in guest RAM (causing CPU readers
such as iconservicesagent on FaceTime's 256x256 0x226 icon surface to
read zero alpha across the icon), while scanout/type-11 RGBA8 readback
decoded Plane 0 without Plane 1 and treated transparent pixels as opaque
black.

Route XR10 IOSurface native writebacks through Rgba16Float encoding into
both Plane 0 and Plane 1, populate Plane 1 on BGRA8/RGBA8 fallback
writes, and decode XR10 IOSurfaces (including Plane 1 alpha on 550/551)
across scanout, type-11 load seeds, type-11 memoized sampling, and
type-5 views.
